    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "No traditional blackout."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary and Joseph are walking home together."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The familiar sound of Nazareth begins before the marketplace is fully visible."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "HAMMER. BASKET. FABRIC SNAP. CLAP."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The same work vocabulary from Scene 1."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The same stalls. The same baskets. The same fabric. The same people."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "For a breath, it feels like home."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary and Joseph enter at the edge of the marketplace, still holding hands."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "One villager notices."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Then another."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A conversation slows."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A woman stops folding fabric."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A merchant looks up."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "No one has become a villain. They simply know—or think they know."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary feels the change in the room before anyone says anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Her hand tightens around Joseph’s."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph answers with his own."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "They keep walking."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "THE CHILDREN BREAK THE TENSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Mary!"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Nia runs toward her before an adult can stop her."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Simon follows, more cautiously. Several children trail behind."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "VILLAGER WOMAN 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Nia—"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Too late."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You’re back!"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I’m back."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Simon looks at Mary. Then Joseph. Then Mary again."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Is it true?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "VILLAGER WOMAN 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Simon!"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "What?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You cannot just ask people things like that."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You were going to ask."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I was going to ask better."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary cannot help a small laugh."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "It’s all right."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Are you really having a baby?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary looks briefly at Joseph, then back to the children."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The children light up immediately."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "No scandal. No hesitation. Just a baby."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "A boy or a girl?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "A boy."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "When is he coming?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Babies do not tell you that."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "How do you know?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Everybody knows that."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You didn’t even know where babies—"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Nia!"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A few adults react. Mary covers another laugh. Joseph does too."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "What will he be like?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary pauses."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I don’t know."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "You don’t?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Not yet."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will he be loud?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "All babies are loud."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Maybe he’ll like stories."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Maybe he’ll build things."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The child looks toward Joseph."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Like you."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph is caught off guard—not by the question, but by the future inside it."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Maybe."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will you teach him?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph looks at Mary."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "This time he does not avoid the answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "If he wants to learn, I’ll teach him."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "What if he’s terrible at it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Then I’ll teach him twice."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The children laugh."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "A light musical pulse begins."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "What do you think he’ll be?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "“WHAT WILL HE BE?” BEGINS"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "“WHAT WILL HE BE?” — MUSICAL TERRITORY"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The children lead. Warm, playful, imaginative. The number is entirely about possibility."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The adults remain in the marketplace, some working, some watching, some whispering."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The song must not explain who Jesus becomes. The audience supplies that knowledge."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "LYRICAL TERRITORY — NOT FINAL LYRICS"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "INTRO"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will he laugh too loud? / Will he sleep all day?"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will he race through every market stall / and leave his things in everybody’s way?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will he love stories?"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "SIMON"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will he climb trees?"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "NIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will he ask a hundred questions / before anyone can breathe?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "CHORUS 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "What will he be? What will he be?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "When he is born, for all to see?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Will he be different or the same?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Will the whole world know his name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "What will he be? What will he be?"
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "The children imagine ordinary futures: animals, stories, running, helping, learning, teaching, courage, kindness."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "VERSE 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will he build things out of wood?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Maybe."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Make a chair that’s strong and good?"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "I hope."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Will you teach him everything?"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Joseph looks at the child, then at Mary."
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "Everything I know."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CHILD 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "That’s Good!"
    },
